  "summary": "The code review identified 5 issues, primarily focusing on a critical XSS vulnerability and poor maintainability practices. The overall code health is low due to lack of input sanitization and missing type safety. The fixed code implements input validation, sanitization, and proper response headers.",
  "fixed_code": "from flask import Flask, request, make_response, Response\nfrom markupsafe import escape\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(\"/profile\")\ndef profile() -> Response:\n    \"\"\"\n    Retrieves the username from query parameters and returns a sanitized response.\n\n    Returns:\n        Response: A Flask response object containing the sanitized username.\n    \"\"\"\n    username = request.args.get('username')\n    if not username:\n        return make_response('Username required', 400)\n    \n    sanitized_username = escape(username)\n    response = make_response(sanitized_username)\n    response.headers['Content-Type'] = 'text/plain; charset=utf-8'\n    return response"
